{"c":[{"id":"b9c59a7dd2810fa8","sum":"B25-B29: Ask sentences in planner/says.ts; Jev confidence = top-two margin; routed producers hold offers; Not right = slip source row click; Router 1 flips near 0.5; scope words are allowlists; Fill all writes writes:true handoffs; undo trusts intended values.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0816855b3eb29c3d","sum":"Ask sentences: planner/says.ts; Jev confidence = top-two margin; unrouted producers self-trigger, routed hold offers; Not right = click on the slip's source row; perch is a rim; Router 1 flips near 0.5; failed fills via fillFailed; wait for site.waitForLoad.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5b436031a992daa5","sum":"Ask's sentences: planner/says.ts, sent as error.says. Pin setGeneratorClock offline. Jev Choice confidence = top-two margin. Intent writer: 8k tok/min, space evals 30 s. Unrouted producers self-trigger; routed hold offers (routing.idle). B27 memory sets: evidence/screen/b27.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message, sent as error.says since H5); pin setGeneratorClock in offline measurements. Jev Choice confidence is the top-two margin (0.75 floor ~0.875 winner). Intent writer gpt-oss-120b: 8k tokens/min, space Ask evals 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask's sentences live in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads (since H5 sent as error.says), its detail holds the check's text. Offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold first forms are cut short.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice confidence is the margin between the top two option probabilities (a 0.75 floor needs ~0.875 on the winner). Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min; intents are ~2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1f86caa19701c852","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers (await routing.idle() then routedSettled). Duplicate naps after a merge go at the next note. B27: score B17/B18 memory sets with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94b9c96f4bec8c25","sum":"D2-02: without HelperOptions.routing producers self-trigger (tests, evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on; routed producers hold offers, so await routing.idle() then routedSettled. I4: a merge of two branches that napped the same notes lists them twice until a note refolds.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233858Z-3b9ba7299adc0299","text":"I4: when two merged branches each napped the same notes, git keeps both naps and wake lists their lines twice (T2's 60b138f0/b105c8e9 vs H4's 7234fe4d); summem has no command to drop one, so fold before branching or accept the duplicate.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7e9161a825c4d83","sum":"I4: after a merge with duplicate naps, the next summem note refolds and drops them; write a note and do its naps. B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last name 'none'; score with the relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T234020Z-7134731208a83f08","text":"I4 correction: the next summem note after such a merge re-plans the folds and drops the duplicate naps (one copy left per line, checked with recall); just write a note and do the naps it asks for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dab2f5b7a08bdf02","sum":"U2-B28: Not right is a click on the slip's source row (keyboard: the fact's row in What Caret knows); stand-ins clip; debug JSON omits nil; perch is a rim on the task's window. Router 1 flips near its 0.5 floor; failed fills reach users via fillFailed; wait for site.waitForLoad.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c8d5b05b4e63693d","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row (keyboard: the fact's row in What Caret knows); stand-ins must clip; debug JSON omits nil keys (.get()); the perch is a rim on the task's window, drawn only while uncovered.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a6b54378f08f606c","sum":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget); its keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows. Off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, or the knows window's footer falls out of renders.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0878a22fa544c193","text":"U2: Not right on an offer is a click on the slip's source row only (NotRightTarget, a tiny click panel over that row); no key is claimed, and the keyboard path is the fact's row in What Caret knows.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-0ab9ad748298511d","text":"U2: SwiftUI's off-screen stand-ins (ScrollingColumn) must take the height offered and clip, as a GeometryReader does; a fixed-size stack in a flexible frame pushed the knows window's footer out of renders.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"52b95150f4d0fe88","sum":"U2: debug JSON omits nil keys (read with .get()); the perch is a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says it is uncovered; corner perch and perch-avoid are gone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T000002Z-69ceb492909786b0","text":"U2: the host's debug JSON leaves out nil keys (synthesized Codable), so a script must read them with .get(); memory_documents_walk.py misread a closed editor as still open.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T000002Z-b1b1695c4d5b6282","text":"U2: the perch is now a rim, perch and caption on the task's own window, drawn only while Rim.seen says nothing covers it; the corner perch, PerchPlacement and perch-avoid are gone (perch-avoid now answers with an error).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"49622ae7d74e40f9","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 flips near its 0.5 floor between runs, so diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: failed fills reach users only via Helper.fillFailed. B28: wait for site.waitForLoad after navigation; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (use fake-app.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ccba801a8aa9c8ea","sum":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between corpus runs; diff per moment before crediting a recall move. B27: a failed fill reaches the user only via Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); ids go to warn.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T031924Z-459c6ef9ec89ae5d","text":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs (m02 0.52/0.49, m09 0.45/0.51); diff runs per moment before crediting a code change with a recall move.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T032639Z-5905894b0fafbfcc","text":"B27: a failed fill reaches the user only through Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); its window and field ids go to warn. Early exits that called this.error published ids until afadd34.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"91fb33162eeab888","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates, wait for site.waitForLoad before the next site.command; accept.ts cannot run executor.run (watchInput gets noWindow), so test page-link VerbResults there and the executor with test/fake-app.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044215Z-74ca06dede7d18b3","text":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or the command goes to the departing page's long poll and times out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T044215Z-8ef7ae66324e8796","text":"B28: accept.ts cannot run executor.run: it first asks the native reader for watchInput and gets noWindow; check page-link VerbResults in accept and the executor with test/fake-app.ts knobs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"09bf3ebde9a35d91","sum":"B28-B29: Ask scope words are allowlists; controls never ride FillField.value, Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true, ticks by boxKind; FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE = PAGE_SUBROLE.file; runs need watchInput ok; undo trusts intended values; choices go to askChoices consumers.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fe681129ca145b17","sum":"B28-D2-04: Ask scope words are allowlists (whole grammar sentence only; EXCLUSION_WORDS drop name trust); accept.ts attach checks need a quiet Mac; controls never ride FillField.value, Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true, ticks by boxKind; radio peers by form owner.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"4b0ed465d296cebd","sum":"B28-I5: Ask scope words are allowlists; whole-form or section scope only for a whole grammar sentence; EXCLUSION_WORDS drop name trust; SECTION trusts fields of its meaning only. accept.ts attach checks need a quiet Mac (10 s timeout).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2fcc93ff7d0331d","sum":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists; a whole-form or section scope is trusted only when the whole normalized instruction is a grammar sentence, a section only under one un-nested heading of the user's own. Searching inside failed open 8 times.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044915Z-bf6a7f62ff27c59b","text":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: only FILLER may stand beside a whole-form or section phrase, and a source phrase must open with a preposition. Matching field labels in the rest failed open three times.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T060231Z-5982020e0a78f148","text":"B28: Ask trusts a whole-form or section scope only if the whole normalized instruction is a scope-words.ts grammar sentence, and a section only under one un-nested heading that is wholly the user's own. Searching inside after stripping sources/titles/quotes failed open 5 times.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"13bd30baef5a6991","sum":"B28b-I5: an Ask with an EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust; a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning. accept.ts --host-app's 1.5 MB attach checks pass the engine's 10 s timeout only on a quiet Mac (5-10 s at load 45); rerun when quiet.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T063813Z-3bd79ae87e6b8e79","text":"B28b: an Ask instruction with a scope-words.ts EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust (Jev confirms every field); a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning (isContactField; up top, my details: none). Restriction word lists stay open; each review found more.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T064425Z-3cff2ff04b6480fa","text":"I5: accept.ts --host-app's three 1.5 MB attach checks slow with load (I4 ~2 s each; load ~45: 5.1, 8.7, >10 s) vs the engine's 10 s timeout. The no-input drop ships the whole file before attach.ts refuses it, so it fails first; rerun when quiet.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0c305010b2d5a883","sum":"D2-04: controls never ride FillField.value; Fill all writes handoffs with writes:true; ticks by boxKind only (never widen by words); accept.ts runs executor tasks on page windows; radio peers by name and form owner, tree-wide.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"499a4d2aad1ced50","sum":"D2-04: a control's value never rides FillField.value; a Fill all writes controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true (writtenFields). A box is ticked by its label's kind (boxKind: only a question to the user); consent word lists failed open twice, so never widen by words alone.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080809Z-f16da6d6064b889b","text":"D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value (zod and the host decoder refuse it on any control but text); a Fill all writes the controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true, through writtenFields.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0265fdcfcf17917c","text":"D2-04: a box gets a tick by its label's kind (fill/controls.ts boxKind: only a question to the user may be written, a first-person statement never gets a value); consent word lists failed open in both reviews, so never widen the box rule by adding words alone.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"63c022257923320b","sum":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's limit is gone); find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner, since a button can join its form through the form attribute.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0557296abbc22e11","text":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept now runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's 'accept cannot run executor.run' no longer holds); page input still comes from the extension's guard.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-c2d09e45a7621952","text":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner: a button outside its form element joins it through the form attribute. The walker's radioPeers and the content script's otherChecked both searched the form element only.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e46d241c907c7f97","sum":"H5-B29: protocol lines round-trip in the reader, host-only ones in host.ndjson; FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE = PAGE_SUBROLE.file; runs need watchInput ok; ledger 'after' is the intended value; numbers compare by canonicalDecimal; choices go only to askChoices consumers.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b09b974152313c33","sum":"H5-B29: protocol.ndjson lines round-trip in the reader, host-only lines in host.ndjson; file inputs carry FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE (= PAGE_SUBROLE.file since H6); runs need watchInput ok; a ledger 'after' is the intended value, a differing read-back blocks undo.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"62ee8c52d89713b7","sum":"H5: reader Swift tests round-trip every protocol.ndjson line; helper-host-only lines go in host.ndjson. Chrome shows a file input as AXButton; page-link marks it FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE, which is PAGE_SUBROLE.file ('CaretFileInput') since H6's merge.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T081037Z-26c2ee6e4f3a2b49","text":"H5: the reader's Swift tests decode and re-encode every line of helper/fixtures/golden/protocol.ndjson; lines only the helper and the host speak go in helper/fixtures/golden/host.ndjson, which both read by path.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T081038Z-3552e4cc7d35ed42","text":"H5: Chrome's AX shows a file input as a plain AXButton; page-link marks page file inputs with subrole caretFileInput (FILE_INPUT_SUBROLE), which validate.ts and planner/attach.ts require for fileAttached steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f3f18eac67e68cd6","sum":"H5-B29: an executor run stops unless the reader answers watchInput ok (accept.ts's noReader answers it via e.reader); a write's ledger 'after' is the intended value, and a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput, which undo refuses.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T081038Z-d40e9fcab32c6674","text":"H5: an executor run stops at once unless the reader link answers watchInput ok; accept.ts's fixture noReader answers noWindow, so a run there (the confirm-file check) answers watchInput itself via e.reader.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092126Z-f0c295d458383a43","text":"B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the value Caret meant to write; a read-back that differs sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it. Journal rows without afterIntended (saved before B29) recover their confirmed writes as mayIncludeInput.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2b825510be0b4a07","sum":"B29: number fields compare by canonicalDecimal for undo; 'without using X' restricts sources (tests say 'not from X'); a continued Ask checks fieldSeen around fill's Jev calls; choices go only to askChoices consumers (the host since H6).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"33a32dbecb06c39a","sum":"B29: page number fields (PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity through canonicalDecimal (Number() merged 2^53+1 with 2^53); sources.ts RESTRICTS matches 'without using X' too, so excluded-source tests say 'not from X'.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2a54c50194565255","text":"B29: page number fields (type=number, inputmode numeric/decimal -> PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity only, through executor.ts canonicalDecimal; Number() made 9007199254740993 equal 9007199254740992.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2d5fb1876e453777","text":"B29: sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X', and such an instruction gets no source question; tests of an excluded source window use 'not from X'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c75543de1b1c0e8","sum":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form via ask.ts fieldSeen (add whatever fill starts reading); questions with choices go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices (the host since H6); AskAsks extends AskRefused for older callers.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2ff420afa6ce639a","text":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen, checked before and after the fill's Jev calls; three reviews each found something fill reads that the record missed, so add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-c755285b7eff0669","text":"B29: Ask questions with choices (planner/choices.ts) go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; AskAsks extends AskRefused, so any other caller reads the old refusal sentence.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c895e0a6f9e3413e","sum":"H6-G2: VM walks judged by results.json; goal steps only via goalAccept, presses hand off; drafts are whole facts; pid-posted keys skip the tap; guest file URLs name real files; stop the router before Helper.shutdown; Router 1 notes in routing/; goals done with left[] empty.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fe8ea3764a8fcfad","sum":"H6-B30: judge VM walks by results.json; alternatives never withdraw for room; goal steps only via goalAccept, presses hand off; drafts are whole facts; router errors are a missed budget; pid-posted keys skip the tap; unreadable clipboard items refuse paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dbb04edae3a352a3","sum":"H7: judge a18_vm_walk.py results.json with vm_results.py; TextEdit fix ⌘Z is one pid-directed ⌘Z; alternatives never withdraw for room. D2-06/V1b: goal steps only via goalAccept, presses hand off, GoalRuns.blocked null after a segment; unreadable clipboard items refuse paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"238a84aaa66db02b","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after each check (judge with vm_results.py); TextEdit writing-fix ⌘Z is one pid-directed ⌘Z, others AX restore; alternatives never withdraw for room (inline or capsule); undrawn offers withdraw; late draws publish(shown:false)+reveal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1cb02aaa5824eced","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check (judge with vm_results.py, test with test_a18_vm_walk.py); a writing fix's Cmd-Z in TextEdit is one pid-directed Cmd-Z (nativeUndo) with no AX restore after; other apps keep the AX restore.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T102528Z-49569322ff77aac5","text":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check and in finally; VM jobs judge it with scripts/vm_results.py, never the transcript's last line. test_a18_vm_walk.py runs the walk against stand-ins on any Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T102528Z-b2fd96251e54b1a0","text":"H7: a writing fix's ⌘Z in TextEdit sends TextEdit one pid-directed ⌘Z (UndoGrant.strategy nativeUndo, NativeUndoApps); nothing restores text after it is sent. Other apps keep the AX restore, which TextEdit-like apps record as a new undo step.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"95ce68e7dc925e47","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py results.json is judged by vm_results.py; alternatives never withdraw for room (fitsInField picks inline or capsule, capsules below the caret line else above); undrawn offers withdraw; drawn-after-publish uses publish(shown: false) + reveal.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T102543Z-0a3850ef6a0fa08f","text":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check and in finally; VM jobs judge it with scripts/vm_results.py, not the transcript tail. test_a18_vm_walk.py runs the walk against stand-ins on any Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T102543Z-4af89305464255b2","text":"H7: alternatives never withdraw for want of inline room: fitsInField picks inline or capsule; CaretLinePlacement puts capsules below the caret line, else above. Undrawn offers withdraw (notDrawn); offers drawn after publish use publish(shown: false) + reveal.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"180a63d9d112870b","sum":"D2-06/V1b: 'Continue' never classified; goal press only e:reveal on 'Next'; page presses hand off; only goalAccept runs goal steps, no taskControl resume; GoalRuns.blocked must go null after a segment or undo fails. Unreadable clipboard items refuse the paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cf5de0df55b6d70e","sum":"D2-06: 'Continue' is unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive dialogs); the one goal press is e:reveal on a whole 'Next'; page presses hand off. Only goalAccept runs a goal's steps; taskControl never resumes one; targets are Target.exact, no fallback.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1712f90f65a11b14","text":"D2-06: 'Continue' is deliberately unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive macOS dialogs); the one goal press capability is e:reveal on a whole 'Next' (goals/capabilities.ts). Page presses are always hand-offs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1ba2dff3c7f2e7e3","text":"D2-06: only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs a goal's steps; a goal task (GoalRuns.owns) is never resumed by taskControl, and a pause stops it. Goal targets are Target.exact (key+role, a button's label): resolveLocally never falls back for them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2fca48002a55d2e6","sum":"D2-06/V1b: GoalRuns.blocked (inside authorize before every act) must return null once a segment ends, or goal undo is refused. A clipboard item with no readable type (a lone public.file-url) refuses the paste; lastInsertion.clipboardTypes shows what was saved.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105431Z-2d9978b4db29946e","text":"D2-06: GoalRuns.blocked runs inside Helper.authorize before every act; it must return null once a segment ends, or a goal task's undo (undoBlocked -> authorize) is refused.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T110217Z-f50d1fce02c90ec1","text":"V1b: Caret pasted over a clipboard whose 2nd item held only public.file-url and the restore dropped it, reporting restored. Items with no readable type now refuse the paste; lastInsertion.clipboardTypes shows what Caret's save read.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c11a295989bc0680","sum":"B30-H7b: plan Asks become goals for goal hosts; name regexes stay case-sensitive; drafts are whole facts. Router errors (R2) are the host's missed budget; pid-posted keys skip the tap; RouteFollower binds by text digest; only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"73770d76091cc26a","sum":"B30: plan-route Asks become goals for goal hosts (planAsk goals:true); keep name regexes case-sensitive (i folds \\p{Lu}). Goal writes skip Cc/Bcc/Subject, To = answered From. Drafts checked as whole typed facts; close holes with whole-expression rules.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"eaeefb243874759f","sum":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan becomes a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true -> AskGoal, helper.offerGoal); others keep planTask/planWithCode. A JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to lower case: keep name patterns case-sensitive.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-9e86109ce30422ae","text":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan is offered as a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true returns AskGoal; helper.offerGoal); other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode. planAsk overloads: goals absent/false types as AskDraft.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-b6135cb945f89335","text":"B30: JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to match lower case too; a case-insensitive name pattern let 'Thanks, I'll pay' skip Jev. Keep name patterns case-sensitive.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d827b4876610494b","sum":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc/Subject; To takes only the From of the answered message (drafts.ts senderOf, rechecked at accept). Drafted text is checked as whole typed facts, every digit in a fact; fix holes with whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-c27c662d572bf540","text":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject, and To takes only the From address in the header block of the message the reply window answers (Re: <subject>), rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf). D2-06 scenes rely on mailWindow line 0 being its From header.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120623Z-4f068d6de508aa09","text":"B30: drafted goal text is checked in goals/drafts.ts as whole typed facts; every digit must land in a fact, and a from value ref stands for its source window or memory. Two reviews found recombination holes: add whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ee5e6005a3f942f5","sum":"H6-H7b: pid-posted keys skip the tap (route through debug 'key char:x' to stamp latency); a router error is outcome error (R2), a missed budget for the host; bindings from sha256(text+NUL+'unknown') digests; only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots the clipboard.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"54a198c67235f383","sum":"H6: pid-posted keys skip the host tap (no latency stamp); ghost_latency_routing.py routes each key through debug 'key char:x' first. Since R2/H8 a failed router call is outcome error + failure, and RouteFollower treats it as that context's missed budget.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T132640Z-116806e783493150","text":"H6: keys posted with CGEventPostToPid never pass the host's event tap, so its latency recorder gets no key stamp; ghost_latency_routing.py routes each key through the debug hook 'key char:x' first, which stamps it, then posts it to the fixture.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T132640Z-ec39615ba3d313e7","text":"H6: the helper publishes a failed or low-confidence router call as a plain abstain (no reason on the wire), so the host cannot fall back on a router error; only a decision that never arrives triggers RouteFollower's budget fallback.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"40260a53530a61ef","sum":"H6: RouteFollower binds the reader's window id/key from a decision whose textRevision is sha256(text+NUL+'unknown')[:16]; empty fields stay tentative. H7b: only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots; every posted key asks mayPost; restored = byte-for-byte re-read.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T132833Z-3831e1a92c996341","text":"H6: the host can't compute the reader's window id/key; RouteFollower binds them from a routeDecision whose textRevision is sha256(text+NUL+'unknown')[:16]. Empty fields share that digest, so their binding stays tentative until the host's revision is echoed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T133211Z-54e0f06319860375","text":"H7b: only ReconcilingClipboard.check makes a ClipboardSnapshot; the executor arms it before KeyType's inserter, every posted key asks mayPost, and restored means a fresh read at the restore's own count matched type for type, byte for byte.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dcd30d5c9d57bc88","sum":"H6-G2: guest file URLs name real files; stop the router before Helper.shutdown; ghost runs use a fresh TextEdit; rig cua-driver alerts cover windows; replayed typing needs value+focusedKey together; Router 1 notes in routing/; goals done only with left[] empty.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"af620a5eca93aec7","sum":"H6-R3: guest file URLs must name real files; stop the router before Helper.shutdown; ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit; rig cua-driver alerts cover windows; replayed typing needs value+focusedKey in one snapshot; corpus incoming-line moments use the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"968935f1f64b4697","sum":"H6-H7b: guest file URLs: seed real files as Finder does; stop the router before Helper.shutdown in scripts; on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit; in the rig, cua-driver get_window_state raises a covering alert, so read AX with a17-tool value.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f9874c6fb70cb129","sum":"H7b: in the VM a public.file-url naming a missing file is seen only by its writer; seed file URLs as Finder does. H6: Helper.shutdown leaves the router live: in-process scripts stop it first (routing_option.ts stop), or a late observe hits closed stores.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T133211Z-f47f4f8a4eaf4829","text":"H7b: on the VM guest's general pasteboard a public.file-url naming a missing file is seen only by its writer; other processes (Caret, a17-tool dump) never list it, count unchanged (A17 race00, plain05-09). Seed file URLs as Finder does: NSURL of a real file.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T143020Z-7e9c54758649b0bf","text":"H6: Helper.shutdown leaves the router live: in-process scripts stop it first (routing_option.ts stop: shadow, cancel timers, await idle), or a late observe hits closed stores and ends the run ('statement has been finalized').","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2bbdec88d0b9e745","sum":"H6/H7b: on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit (caret-fixture's field gave few value reads). In the rig guest cua-driver get_window_state raises a bypass alert that covers windows (offers held covered); read AX with a17-tool value.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T143020Z-8eb592e9f22ab7a6","text":"H6: on-screen ghost runs type into a fresh TextEdit instance; caret-fixture's single-line field gave the host almost no value reads. With pid-posted keys both reader and host saw TextEdit's field come and go 20+ times in 130 keys.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T152850Z-7c0a9e0204dd886b","text":"H7b: in the rig guest, cua-driver get_window_state raises macOS's 'CuaDriver ... bypass the system private window picker' alert (UserNotificationCenter, layer 8); it stays up and covers windows, so Caret holds offers as covered. Read AX values with a17-tool value.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ac3096d5776075d7","sum":"R2-R3 routing: replayed typing needs its value in the same snapshot; no focusedKey makes Router 1 abstain; Router 1 skipped only for consentedCandidates offers (routing/consent.ts); run incoming-line corpus moments on the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8c07db9d1f57e7f4","sum":"R2: replayed typing must carry its typed value in the same snapshot as the text, or no breakpoint opens and no event card lists; a recorded snapshot without focusedKey makes Router 1 abstain (A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155131Z-2d735fed11dec073","text":"R2: scripts that replay typing must send a typed value (snapshot values) in the same snapshot as its text: a value that arrives after the sentence boundary opens no breakpoint, so the event card is never listed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T155131Z-b3055d198779a6ea","text":"R2: a recorded snapshot without the reader's focusedKey makes Router 1 read 'the cursor is not in a text field' and abstain; A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47, which is why H6 saw the loop abstain.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3b5d87e819a193ac","sum":"R2-R3: Router 1 is skipped only for offers consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's record (routing/consent.ts; those messages count only from a host session); corpus-eval --real-clock never waits the router cooldown, so run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155145Z-05c6fed3ed39acff","text":"R2: Router 1 is skipped only for offers Helper.consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's own record (routing/consent.ts). Messages that write such records (skillAnswer, resume, skills/ save, watch role) count only from a host session.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-3e0249266797e51f","text":"R3: corpus-eval --real-clock settle() does not wait the router cooldown timer, so an incoming line's later context is never scored; run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"592a384cd6680d71","sum":"R3-G2: jev.holding tests await a flush; Jev judges state on short criteria; Router 1's task question is separate; no routingContext for a plain caret; goals done only with left[] empty; pick goal values by quoted part; goal writes pass goals/gates.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"71181bfecc426109","sum":"R3: await a flush not coord.idle() under jev.holding; Jev judges state against short criteria (rule in instructions); Router 1's task question is a separate request; corpus m36/m43/m37 misses are event-card code, not the router.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5a582d7c7a76d2a6","sum":"R3: with jev.holding, await a flush not coord.idle() (a stale reply frees the slot); Jev judges the request state against short criteria: what it judges goes in state, the rule in instructions (task question with the sentence in the act option split ~50/50).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-4f977dd1bf6c45f7","text":"R3: coordinator tests with jev.holding: a stale reply now frees the slot and the next field's call starts at once, so await a flush, not coord.idle(), while a call is held (idle would wait on the held call).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-539f47d0a41290db","text":"R3: Jev (System One) judges the request state against short criteria; put what it judges in state and the rule in instructions. Router 1's task question with the sentence inside the act option split ~50/50 (r3 task-wording probe 8/14 vs 14/14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a2301c765553cede","sum":"R3: Router 1's task question is its own request after the outcome question (one shared state moved m34 write 0.75 to 0.32); corpus m36/m43/m37 misses are event-card code (no date anchor, no person), not the router.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-75585e5911775e88","text":"R3: Router 1's task question (judge.ts) is its own request after the outcome question; with the offer in one shared state the outcome answers moved (corpus m34 write 0.75 -> 0.32).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-9c33f255f5c1caad","text":"R3: corpus m36/m43 list no event card by the producer's rule (a conversation line's relative date has no anchor); m37 finds no person. Those misses are event-card code, not the router.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"21f781157288bdd8","sum":"R3-G2: no routingContext for a plain caret ('unknown' reads as caret); goals are done only with left[] empty; pick goal values by their quoted part; every goal write passes goals/gates.ts, and desk tests use test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"711ded7100cb3d56","sum":"R3-G2: RouteFollower sends no routingContext for a plain caret, so context.ts reads 'unknown' as caret; GoalProgress is done only when left[] is empty, and runs.ts owes every required or recipient field left.ts marks in windows a goal writes in.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-dcc2d733c48b884a","text":"R3: RouteFollower sends no routingContext while the selection is a plain caret, so routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as caret; comparing them ended every write session at the host's first sentence end.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-100b242cff553f5d","text":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only when left[] is empty (partial/handoff otherwise); runs.ts owes every field left.ts marks required or recipient in windows a goal writes in, and a closed window leaves them unresolved.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9acdbaecfe2a51ce","sum":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so goal-prompt.ts says pick values by their quoted part; every goal write passes goals/gates.ts, lowerGoal needs askJev + ledger, and desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-33695164e4940cad","text":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so live qwen3.8 matched v.display.includes('ORD-...') to the sender's email; goal-prompt.ts now says pick values by their quoted part.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-c65516aec96de620","text":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit + numberFieldMisfit, Ask's verifyWrites Jev question); lowerGoal is async and needs askJev + ledger; with no Jev a goal writes no copied value, so desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
